<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela nationwide bus strike set for Monday.</title>
<headline>Venezuela nationwide bus strike set for Monday.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's transport union said Friday it would stage a nationwide strike next week if the government did not answer calls for a 50 percent increase in bus fares.</p>
<p>&quot;We're very sorry for the users, but we're in a conflict situation and we won't stop until we have something to offer the workers,&quot; bus union president Raul Maldonado told reporters.</p>
<p>The government had agreed to a 30 percent hike in fares.</p>
<p>But bus drivers in Caracas's suburbs have been on strike since Wednesday after the Transport Ministry turned down requests for a further 20 percent increase.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 834405</p>
</text>
